---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '2026-10-24';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="PromptDNS refund policy: every tool is free. For paid monitoring plans when they launch: 14-day full refund on first payments, handled via Dodo Payments."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Refund policy</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Refund policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-faint">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>The tools are free</h2>
      <p>
        All PromptDNS tools are free and require no account, so there is nothing to refund for
        tool usage - today or ever.
      </p>

      <h2>Paid plans (when they launch)</h2>
      <p>
        Paid monitoring plans are in development. When billing goes live, this policy applies
        from day one:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>14-day full refund on any first payment</strong> of a plan, no questions asked.</li>
        <li><strong>Cancel anytime.</strong> Plans are month-to-month; cancelling keeps monitoring active until the end of the paid period.</li>
        <li>Renewal charges after the first 14 days are refunded pro-rata if the service was non-functional and we could not fix it.</li>
        <li>One-time services (setup or managed work) state their own refund terms in writing before purchase.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How refunds are processed</h2>
      <p>
        Payments will be processed by <strong>Dodo Payments</strong> as our merchant of record.
        Dodo handles the charge, global taxes, and the refund back to your original payment
        method. Requests reach us fastest via
        <a href="mailto:support@promptdns.com" class="text-accent">support@promptdns.com</a> -
        include the email you signed up with and we'll action it within 2 business days.
      </p>

      <h2>Abuse</h2>
      <p>
        We may decline repeated refund-and-resubscribe patterns on the same account. This applies
        to exceptional cases only; a normal first-payment refund is never questioned.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
